<p>Web excursions brought to you in partnership with <a href="https://macpaw.7eer.net/c/228914/82479/1733">CleanMyMac X</a>, all the tools to speed up your Mac, in one app.</p>

<p>Happy 4th of July, for those (in the US) who observe. It&rsquo;s a hot one
here. So I&rsquo;m cooling off with some cool Mac (and one iOS) tools. Please enjoy
responsibly.</p>

<dl>
  <dt><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/senqu-image-converter/id6772722134?mt=12">‎Senqu Image Converter App - App Store</a></dt>
  <dd>Cool, focused little app for image conversion and compression. Read <a href="https://thabodavidnyakalloklass.medium.com/i-got-tired-of-uploading-my-photos-to-random-websites-just-to-convert-them-so-i-built-a-native-mac-e21ae53d6fa7">the launch story</a> to learn more.</dd>
  <dt><a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/powerhouz/id924503714#information">‎PowerHouz App</a></dt>
  <dd>PowerHouz is an iOS app that wraps 26 home automation functions in a sci-fi command deck — neon HUD, sound effects, a surveillance “red alert” mode, the whole Make it so energy.</dd>
  <dd>
    <p>HomeKit accessories, Apple Health rings, calendar, sleep tracking, weather — every panel styled like you’re running a starship bridge. Runs on iPhone, iPad, Apple Watch and Apple TV.</p>
  </dd>
  <dt><a href="https://www.tintd.app/#features">Tintd 2</a></dt>
  <dd>Super cool development for Tintd: it now runs in the background and automatically applies colors and icons based on folder names. Pretty brilliant.</dd>
  <dt><a href="https://indieseek.co/apps/paste-switch/">Paste Switch - Paste Faster on Mac</a></dt>
  <dd>Cool little utility that, as opposed to a standard clipboard manager, cycles through recent pastes as you hit the keyboard shortcut, replacing the insertion. It&rsquo;s the kill ring I&rsquo;ve played with in KeyboardBindings.dict, but covers images and other formats as well.</dd>
  <dt><a href="https://notchkin.app/">Notchkin</a></dt>
  <dd>A really well done little notes app that lives in your notch. Rich text editor with Markdown/RTF export, highlights and checklists, and keyboard shortcuts for everything. It even has #tagging you can use to organize your notes.</dd>
  <dt><a href="https://www.screensnap.pro/">ScreenSnap Pro</a></dt>
  <dd>
    <blockquote>
      <p>ScreenSnap Pro turns plain screenshots into pro visuals — backgrounds, annotations, GIF recording, instant cloud links. One-time purchase.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </dd>
  <dd>
    <p>This looks like a really great app. Not sure anything could ever replace CleanShot for me, but this looks to be a great alternative, and doesn&rsquo;t require a subscription. Trying it out for a while, I&rsquo;ll report back.</p>
  </dd>
</dl>

